//
// The key area (RFC-0075 Phase 8b; design artifacts: OnScreenKeyboard, KeyboardKey): the
// number row and the three letter rows are pure DATA from the keymaps SSOT (`svc.ime.rows`,
// row 0 = digits), then the bottom row. The clipboard's cards take the area's place while
// they are open (TASK-0067B). Every row has the same share of the height, gap 8. The number
// row stays in every size class because the WM's band is one height for all of them — five
// rows of keys fill it. A layout's own rows never branch here.

Component KeyRows {
    Stack {
        KeyRow { cells: $state.row0 }
        KeyRow { cells: $state.row1 }
        KeyRow { cells: $state.row2 }
        ShiftRow { }
        BottomRow { }
    }
    .gap(8)
    .grow(1)
}
